{
  "schema": "ld-s10y-image/figure-spec@2",
  "id": "fig-choice-intersections-FIRST",
  "mode": "deterministic",
  "description": "Four authored graph windows from the complete equations: A solid 2^x vs dashed x+1; B solid .3^x vs dashed x+1; C and D solid 2^x vs dashed x^2-2, respectively negative and positive windows. Both sides are rendered, including the positive near-miss; no root markers, values or answer-bearing labels are added. These are new analytic plots, not invented original scans.",
  "source": {
    "authoredBasis": "Four authored graph windows from the complete equations: A solid 2^x vs dashed x+1; B solid .3^x vs dashed x+1; C and D solid 2^x vs dashed x^2-2, respectively negative and positive windows. Both sides are rendered, including the positive near-miss; no root markers, values or answer-bearing labels are added. These are new analytic plots, not invented original scans.",
    "authoritativeText": [
      {
        "lesson": "alg8-c5-ex",
        "exercise": "698",
        "text": "698. 用图解法解下列方程：\na) $2^x=x+1$；\nb) $(0.3)^x=x+1$."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "alg8-c5-ex",
        "exercise": "699",
        "text": "699. 利用函数 $y=2^x$ 和 $y=x^2-2$ 的图象解方程$2^x=x^2-2$."
      }
    ],
